back, forward or cross edge. Parallel edges are told apart: a repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tree edge is a forward edge at its own position. It holds a copy of the graph and can be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterated more than once. The search keeps its own stack, so a deep graph cannot overflow the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call stack.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearch"}}}